From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] [ofono-binder] Keep the display state in one object for both
 monitors

The two device monitors each read MCE's display state through
libmce-glib and took a state that isn't valid as on. Give them one
shared BinderDisplay instead, which has that rule and gets its state
from a backend. The backend here is MCE, as before; with it the
monitors behave as they did. This is so that the state can come from
somewhere else on a system without MCE.

unit_display replaces unit_devmon, which tested the two helpers that
are now the display object's rule.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
